op four hold 9% of revenue), so pricing power is hard to come by."],"mkt":["The shares are in a strong uptrend, up 35% over the past year excluding the latest month, though it has pulled back 10% over the last three months.","The price sits mid-way through its 52-week range, 24% below the high.","With annualised volatility of 41% and a beta of 1.30, it amplifies market moves, though its beta has shifted (1y 0.82 vs 5y 1.51), so read it loosely.","Liquidity is deep, with about $187.1M traded a day.","In past sell-offs it fell 59% in the 2020 crash, 46% in the 2022 bear market and 53% in 2008."],"val":["The price sits above its DCF fair value of $91.75 (margin of safety -93%), so there is no valuation cushion.","The fair-value models disagree (dispersion 53%), and the Monte Carlo range runs $44.73 to $173 (P10-P90), so treat the estimate as noisy.","On multiples it looks expensive against Industrials peers: P/E 41.6 vs 23.3 and P/FCF 62.7 vs 22.3 (sector median).","Against its own history it is dear: the EBIT multiple sits 230% above its 10-year median.","Earnings yields are thin: an FCF yield of 1.6% (below the risk-free rate) and an EBIT/EV of 2.7% (vs the 8% bar).","The 23 covering analysts target $224 on average, 27% above the price, well away from the model's fair value."],"prof":["ROIC of 9% falls short of the cost of capital of 10.4%, so growth at these returns destroys value; returns have swung a lot from year to year (CV 3.34).","It runs a 17% gross margin and converts 4% of revenue into free cash flow.","Earnings quality is mixed: cash conversion of 3.12x, but high accruals (-8.2% of assets).","ROE of 17% is amplified by 4.4x balance-sheet leverage (DuPont), so ROIC is the cleaner read on the business.","It spends 0.9% of revenue on stock compensation."],"hlth":["Leverage is moderate at 2.6x net debt to EBITDA ($310.0M of cash against $3.3B of debt), above the 1.5x gate, and interest cover is thin at 3.0x."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 1.9% over 3 years, -12.9% over 5 years and 0.7% over 10 years, so growth is accelerating, and it has been lumpy (year-to-year swings of 87%).","At current returns, reinvesting 38% of profits supports about 3.5% a year of fundamental growth, enough to sustain growth.","Free cash flow has compounded -1.7% a year over five years, short of the 5% durability bar.","Forward indicators: a book-to-bill of 0.88 (orders lagging sales), a backlog worth 1% of annual revenue and deferred revenue down 24%.","Capex roughly matches depreciation (1.4x, 8.1% of sales), a maintenance pace.","Its Rule of 40 score is -10, below the 40 that marks a healthy growth business."],"own":["Insiders own a modest 2.2%, and reported institutional holdings exceed 100% of shares (a sign of heavy share lending).","Insiders have only sold over the past year (20 sales, net $3.4M sold).","Shareholder yield is a modest 0.6% (0.6% in buybacks)."],"people":["With about 38,000 employees, each generates about $215K of revenue, 0.6x the Industrials median, and productivity has risen 31.5% a year.","That works out to $9K of free cash flow per employee.","CEO pay is $2.1M (10x revenue per employee), and compensation governance scores well (1/10, lower is better).","Stock compensation averages $2K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"AVOID","conv":30,"head":"Avoid: priced 93% above its fair value of $91.75.","pros":["Altman Z in the safe zone","23 analysts' mean target $224 (+27%)","12-1 month momentum +35%"],"cons":["Trades 93% above fair value of $91.75","ROIC 9.3% vs WACC 10.4%","Revenue shrank 12.9%/yr over 5y","Interest coverage only 3.0x","Fair value is low-confidence (wide Monte Carlo spread)"],"flags":["Priced 93% above its fair value of $91.75"],"need":[],"buy_below":77.99,"vc":{"base":91.75,"base_src":"dcf","bear":44.73,"bull":172.99,"alt_median":27.86,"n_alt":1,"gap":2.2929,"dispersion":0.5341,"level":"LOW","why":["Monte Carlo spread is wide","models disagree (53% dispersion)","DCF is 229% above the other models' medi